3.3 Functional Requirements.
Assessment Functionality (FR1-FR4): 50 item readiness questionnaire for all 5 CE control areas;
individual responses clearly mapped to NCSC/IASME certification criteria; four-point response scale
(Yes=2, Partial=1, No=0, N/A=0); contextual help text for technical language. Scoring and Analysis
(FR5-FR9): total readiness percentage; scores of each CE control area; critical failure conditions
leading to automatic certification failures; prioritised gap analysis with remediation action in terms
of severity; readiness, Ready (>85%), Nearly Ready (70-85%), Significant Gaps (50-70%), Not Ready
(<50%). Templates (FR10-FR16): Password Policy, Remote Access and VPN Policy, Incident Response
Procedure, Device and Access Control Register, Firewall Configuration Checklist, Patch Management
Log, Acceptable Use Policy. Guidance (FR17-FR19): Plain-language remediation guidance per failed
requirement; step-by-step instructions; reference to relevant templates. Dashboard (FR20-FR25):
High-visibility display of overall readiness; radar chart showing per-control readiness; prioritised gap
list with severity indicators; downloadable PDF gap analysis report; direct access to templates based
on gaps; Save/Resume assessment.
