Prioritisation: core functionality and evaluation override enhancement features. If you do have
limited time, features rejected in reverse: (1) Core assessment and scoring [must get done]; (2)
Simulated evaluation and results analysis [must be done]; (3) Export PDFs [should be worked on]; (4)
Save/resume [could be deferred]; (5) Advanced visualisations [can be deferred].
Quality Assurance: All artefacts methodologically tested i.e functional testing
(buttons/links/workflows have all the relevant functionality), calculation testing (scoring engine
produces the expected results), browser testing (the appearance/functionality is the same across all
browsers), accessibility testing (the web interface is also compatible with all major web browsers),
documentation testing (templates are complete in terms of appearance and are professionally
formatted), and usability testing (the pages are always usable!).
